  "claim_boundary": "T19-L is a prospectively frozen endpoint-and-label follow-up on atomic emoji surfaces that may have appeared in earlier repository experiments, plus a text-repository-fresh non-emoji Unicode-symbol control. The alternative label is one exact CLDR keyword whose ASCII-alphanumeric words are disjoint from the canonical CLDR tts words; it is a source-auditable keyword alias, not a human-rated paraphrase. T19-C, if admitted, tests a fixed low-rank representation intervention in one pinned Llama 3.2 3B Transformers/CUDA cell on a bank with zero T19-L forwards. A positive result would support only bounded lexical correspondence and component-level causal contribution under these inputs and endpoints. It cannot establish rendered-glyph perception, human meaning, understanding, a unique or complete circuit, tokenizer independence, pretraining novelty, architecture or model-population generality, a scale law, tuning effects, or natural-language behavior.",
